    "created_at": "2019-03-28T18:47:30Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-03-28T18:47:30Z",
    "body": "So Blink appears to set the container's nested browsing context fairly early -- essentially right after the new browsing context is created, and before the JavaScript execution context is created.\r\n\r\nFor auxiliary browsing contexts, I believe that the opener is also set early: when the new context is created, it is passed its opener frame, if it exists, and this is then used when constructing the document. (Opener is passed in to [create a new browsing context](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/browsers.html#creating-a-new-browsing-context) in the spec as well, so that's not significantly different)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
